# Line endings.
#
# Every .sh in this repository is executed inside a Linux container or by bash on the
# host. A CRLF line ending breaks both: bash reports "\r: command not found", and a
# script piped into `iris session` fails because the CR is read as part of the command.
# The container entrypoint (common/start.sh) is the worst case - the container simply
# will not start.
#
# On a Windows clone Git converts line endings on checkout unless it is told not to,
# so the rule is set here rather than left to each machine's core.autocrlf.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.cpf   text eol=lf
*.conf  text eol=lf
*.ini   text eol=lf

# The PowerShell equivalents run on Windows and are fine with CRLF; PowerShell reads
# LF as well, so this is a convenience, not a requirement.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalise in the repository, check out with the platform's own
# ending. Documentation and Compose files are read by tools that accept both.
*       text=auto

*.docx  binary
*.gif   binary
*.key   binary
